to spoil even further...

(these things I've noticed from my own playing, if it's inaccurate, I  
apologise)

Any sort of fresh, edible meat will tame a dog or cat. Corpses that they  
like (ie not lichen or acid blobs) will tame 'em straight away. Don't try  
to throw tins :P

Lichen, fungi, fruit and vegetables will tame horses.

Throwing horse food at dogs and cats will make them peaceful, the same for  
throwing meat at horses.

Candy bars count as a "meat" food as far as the above is concerned.

Food rations are vegetarian, as far as the #conduct is concerned. BUT  
throwing one at a horse will make it peaceful, and throwing it to a dog or  
cat will make it tame. Tame dogs/cats/horses WON'T eat food rations unless  
they're starving.

For taming dogs and cats, I prefer the last available monster corpse,  
otherwise a precious food ration. Tripe works wonders for training an  
already tame one, and it's a great find early on.

As for dragons and other exotic pets, wand/spell/trap of polymorphing an  
already tame pet works (trap is favourite because it doesn't hurt them),  
otherwise magical taming as already mentioned. Note that it's harder the  
higher level the monster is.

